.page tee 1 copy input to files and to output

# SYNOPSIS
*tee* [*-ai*] [_FILE_...]

# DESCRIPTION
`tee` copies standard input to standard output and also to each _FILE_, which is created or truncated. It is the plumber's T-joint: use it to look at a pipeline while saving what flows through it.

# OPTIONS
@ *-a*
    Append to the files instead of truncating them.
@ *-i*
    Accepted for compatibility; it changes nothing.

If a file cannot be opened a message is printed and the exit status will be 1, but the copying goes on to the remaining outputs.

# EXAMPLES
    dmesg | tee /tmp/boot.log | grep -i usb
    echo "new line" | tee -a notes.txt

# SEE ALSO
cat(1), gapsh-language(7)
